# CETH, Electronic Text Centers, and the Humanities Community.

**Authors:** Gaunt, Marianne

## Abstract
Describes the Center for the Electronic Texts in the Humanities (CETH), a joint project of Princeton University and Rutgers University (New Jersey) to provide a national focus for humanities computing. Examines the evolution of CETH as its role has changed with the growth of the humanities computing community and the impact of the digital environment. (LRW)

